  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\n- {冷|ひ}やす (transitive): to cool (something)\n- ⟦{冷|ひ}える→冷える：01154_hieru⟧ (intransitive): to get cold (on its own)\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- ⟦{頭|あたま}→頭：00574_atama⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{冷|ひ}やす: to cool one's head (calm down)\n- ⟦{肝|きも}→肝：10796_kimo⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{冷|ひ}やす: to be frightened, have a close call\n- ⟦ビール→ビール：01015_biiru⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{冷|ひ}やす: to chill beer\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- ⟦{冷|つめ}たい→冷たい：00681_tsumetai⟧: cold (to the touch)\n- ⟦{冷|さ}める→冷める：02114_sameru⟧: to cool down (intrans., temperature or feelings)\n- ⟦{冷|さ}ます→冷ます：02113_samasu⟧: to let cool, to dampen (enthusiasm)\n\nNote: {冷|ひ}やす focuses on actively cooling something, while ⟦{冷|さ}ます→冷ます：02113_samasu⟧ implies letting something cool naturally.",
